 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508257,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Choose the correct graph for <span data-math=\"y > 3x + 5\">y &gt; 3x + 5</span>.\n<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/4b598f50808fe4f0.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 5. The line passes through the points, (negative 2, negative 5) and (0, 2.5). The region to the right of the line is shaded. Note: all values are approximate.\">\n\n<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/a45183a9043270ea.png\" alt=\"A dashed line is plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 5. The line passes through the points, (negative 2, negative 5) and (0, 2.5). The region to the right of the line is shaded. Note: all values are approximate.\">\n\n<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/8360b1ab9b2fa95a.png\" alt=\"\">\n\n<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/61729ee2c25e7265.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 5. The line passes through the points, (negative 2, negative 5) and (0, 2.5). The region to the left of the line is shaded. Note: all values are approximate.\">\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Graph the inequality, and then compare it to the options.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y > 3x + 5\"></span></p>\n<p>Graph the line <span data-math=\"y = 3x + 5\"></span> with a dotted line, since this is a strictly greater than inequality.</p>\n<p>Shade above the line since this is a “<i>y</i> &gt;”.</p>\n<p>Test <span data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span> to be sure you shaded correctly.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 > 3\\left( 0 \\right) + 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 > 5\"></span> is false, so this ordered pair is not on the line. <span data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span> should not be in the shaded area. You shaded correctly.</p>\n<p>Two points are all it takes to determine a line, so this is the correct equation for the line.</p>\n<p>The correct graph is the third graph.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBc2dPIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--f3f424d600bf64696fc5072090a7fbc8dc63ed67/CS_Figure_05_05_034.png\" alt=\"A dashed line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 10 to 10 in increments of 2.5. The line passes through the following points, (negative 2.5, negative 10) and (0, 2.5). The region above the line is shaded. Note: all values are approximate.\">"
    }
   ],
